Subject: [PATCH] gdb/macrotab: catch exception and rethrow around
 splay_tree_foreach

Bug 34876 talks about a crash that happens with "-O3 -flto", when
completing and reaching the maximum number of completions.

It can be reproduced by building GDB in this configuration:

    $ ./configure CFLAGS="-march=x86-64-v3 -flto -O3" CXXFLAGS="-march=x86-64-v3 -flto -O3" --disable-nls

Then, using a dummy C program compiled with "gcc -g3", this crashes GDB:

    $ ./gdb -q -nx --data-directory data-directory ./a.out -ex list -ex "complete macro expand "

The crash manifests as an invalid free, reported by glibc:

    free(): invalid pointer

