I asked Claude to find the root cause, and it came up with the following
explanation:

  1. With -batch, or after 200 matches interactively,
     completion_tracker::add_completion throws
     MAX_COMPLETIONS_REACHED_ERROR.

  2. That throw happens inside the add_macro_name callback, which is called
     from libiberty's splay_tree_foreach (C code) via
     foreach_macro_in_scope in gdb/macrotab.c.

  3. libiberty is compiled as C without -fexceptions, so GCC treats
     splay_tree_foreach as nothrow. With LTO, GCC can see that across
     translation units, so it decides macro_for_each_in_scope can't throw
     either. It then compiles the call at symtab.c:6052 as non-throwing.

  4. At runtime the exception still unwinds, because x86-64 has CFI
     everywhere. But it lands in a landing pad that doesn't belong to that
     call site. That pad runs ~lookup_name_info() with this = %rbx. At the
     throwing call, %rbx actually holds the function_view invoker address
     (0x555555b32780, a code address), so it destroys garbage and hands a
     bogus pointer to free().

I can't tell for sure that it's correct, but it sounds very plausible to
me (the address 0x555555b32780 is from another run on another computer, not
related to the backtrace above).

On x86-64, the psABI mandates that all programs and libraries have an async
unwind table (.eh_frame), so the exception is able to go through the C
frames unnoticed most of the time.  But on ARM, for example, programs don't
have unwind tables by default.  I was able to reproduce the bug on my old
Raspberry Pi running an outdated Debian:

    (gdb) show version
    GNU gdb (Raspbian 10.1-1.7) 10.1.90.20210103-git
    ...
    (gdb) list
    1	int main()
    2	{
    3	}
    (gdb) complete macro expand
    terminate called after throwing an instance of 'gdb_exception_error'
    Aborted

There, the exception causes std::terminate to be called as soon as it
reaches the libiberty C frame.

This patch updates the two callbacks passed to splay_tree_foreach in
this file (foreach_macro and foreach_macro_in_scope) to catch any
exception that would escape, stash it in macro_for_each_data::exception,
and return 1 to stop the splay tree iteration.  The caller of
splay_tree_foreach then rethrows the exception if there is one.

Since I'm re-indenting the code anyway, I took the opportunity to
modernize it a bit.

Improve gdb.base/macscp.exp to kind of cover this.  The test won't catch
the bug on a regular x86-64 build, but it would in an LTO build like in
the bug report, or on ARM without unwind tables.  It would also catch it
if we just added "noexcept" to the callbacks.

There is another latent instance of this bug in addrmap.c, where we call
splay_tree_foreach and the callback can throw.  And probably more when
using other APIs.  As future work, I propose that we go over all the
callbacks that we pass to a C API to mark them "noexcept", so that these
cases of exceptions crossing C frames consistently crash GDB on any
configuration.  And fix them if necessary to catch and rethrow
exceptions like done in this patch.

Change-Id: Ie7c4515a4dee1c93b04271f1d5057be23c96c039
Bug: https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=34876
Approved-By: Andrew Burgess <aburgess@redhat.com>
---
 gdb/macrotab.c                    | 75 ++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 gdb/testsuite/gdb.base/macscp.exp | 27 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 76 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gdb/macrotab.c b/gdb/macrotab.c
index 078eb5cb..ef5b700b 100644
--- a/gdb/macrotab.c
+++ b/gdb/macrotab.c
@@ -945,22 +945,31 @@ struct macro_for_each_data
   gdb::function_view<macro_callback_fn> fn;
   struct macro_source_file *file;
   int line;
+  std::exception_ptr exception;
 };
 
 /* Helper function for macro_for_each.  */
 static int
-foreach_macro (splay_tree_node node, void *arg)
+foreach_macro (splay_tree_node node, void *arg) noexcept
 {
-  struct macro_for_each_data *datum = (struct macro_for_each_data *) arg;
-  struct macro_key *key = (struct macro_key *) node->key;
-  struct macro_definition *def;
+  auto datum = static_cast<macro_for_each_data *> (arg);
 
-  std::string key_fullname = macro_source_fullname (key->start_file);
-  def = fixup_definition (key_fullname.c_str (), key->start_line,
-			  (struct macro_definition *) node->value);
+  try
+    {
+      auto key = reinterpret_cast<macro_key *> (node->key);
+      auto value = reinterpret_cast<macro_definition *> (node->value);
+      std::string key_fullname = macro_source_fullname (key->start_file);
+      macro_definition *def = fixup_definition (key_fullname.c_str (),
+						key->start_line, value);
 
-  datum->fn (key->name, def, key->start_file, key->start_line);
-  return 0;
+      datum->fn (key->name, def, key->start_file, key->start_line);
+      return 0;
+    }
+  catch (...)
+    {
+      datum->exception = std::current_exception ();
+      return 1;
+    }
 }
 
 /* Call FN for every macro in TABLE.  */
@@ -971,31 +980,42 @@ macro_for_each (struct macro_table *table,
   struct macro_for_each_data datum;
 
   datum.fn = fn;
-  datum.file = NULL;
+  datum.file = nullptr;
   datum.line = 0;
   splay_tree_foreach (table->definitions, foreach_macro, &datum);
+
+  if (datum.exception != nullptr)
+    std::rethrow_exception (datum.exception);
 }
 
 static int
-foreach_macro_in_scope (splay_tree_node node, void *info)
+foreach_macro_in_scope (splay_tree_node node, void *info) noexcept
 {
-  struct macro_for_each_data *datum = (struct macro_for_each_data *) info;
-  struct macro_key *key = (struct macro_key *) node->key;
-  struct macro_definition *def;
+  auto datum = static_cast<macro_for_each_data *> (info);
 
-  std::string datum_fullname = macro_source_fullname (datum->file);
-  def = fixup_definition (datum_fullname.c_str (), datum->line,
-			  (struct macro_definition *) node->value);
+  try
+    {
+      auto key = reinterpret_cast<macro_key *> (node->key);
+      auto value = reinterpret_cast<macro_definition *> (node->value);
+      std::string datum_fullname = macro_source_fullname (datum->file);
+      macro_definition *def = fixup_definition (datum_fullname.c_str (),
+						datum->line, value);
 
-  /* See if this macro is defined before the passed-in line, and
-     extends past that line.  */
-  if (compare_locations (key->start_file, key->start_line,
-			 datum->file, datum->line) < 0
-      && (!key->end_file
-	  || compare_locations (key->end_file, key->end_line,
-				datum->file, datum->line) >= 0))
-    datum->fn (key->name, def, key->start_file, key->start_line);
-  return 0;
+      /* See if this macro is defined before the passed-in line, and
+	 extends past that line.  */
+      if (compare_locations (key->start_file, key->start_line,
+			     datum->file, datum->line) < 0
+	  && (key->end_file == nullptr
+	      || compare_locations (key->end_file, key->end_line,
+				    datum->file, datum->line) >= 0))
+	datum->fn (key->name, def, key->start_file, key->start_line);
+      return 0;
+    }
+  catch (...)
+    {
+      datum->exception = std::current_exception ();
+      return 1;
+    }
 }
 
 /* Call FN for every macro is visible in SCOPE.  */
@@ -1010,6 +1030,9 @@ macro_for_each_in_scope (struct macro_source_file *file, int line,
   datum.line = line;
   splay_tree_foreach (file->table->definitions,
 		      foreach_macro_in_scope, &datum);
+
+  if (datum.exception != nullptr)
+    std::rethrow_exception (datum.exception);
 }
 
 
diff --git a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.base/macscp.exp b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.base/macscp.exp
index e40bfb63..e0bcddb9 100644
--- a/gdb/testsuite/gdb.base/macscp.exp
+++ b/gdb/testsuite/gdb.base/macscp.exp
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 # You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
 # along with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 
+load_lib completion-support.exp
 
 standard_testfile macscp1.c
 set objfile [standard_output_file ${testfile}.o]
@@ -750,3 +751,29 @@ gdb_test "macro expand siginfo.si_addr" \
 gdb_test "print __FILE__" " = \".*macscp1.c\""
 gdb_test "print __LINE__" \
     " = [gdb_get_line_number {stopping point for line test}]"
+
+# Regression test for bug 34876.
+
+with_test_prefix "max-completions reached" {
+    with_set max-completions 2 {
+	# Macros from the program, visited by foreach_macro_in_scope.  All
+	# the BEFORE_<func> macros are in scope at this point.  The macros
+	# are visited in alphabetical order.
+	test_gdb_complete_multiple "macro expand " "BEFORE_" "MACSCP1_" {
+	    "BEFORE_MACSCP1_1"
+	    "BEFORE_MACSCP1_2"
+	} "" "" true "program macros"
+
+	# User-defined macros, visited by foreach_macro.
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro define USER_MACRO_A 1"
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro define USER_MACRO_B 2"
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro define USER_MACRO_C 3"
+	test_gdb_complete_multiple "macro expand " "USER_MACRO_" "" {
+	    "USER_MACRO_A"
+	    "USER_MACRO_B"
+	} "" "" true "user macros"
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro undef USER_MACRO_A"
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro undef USER_MACRO_B"
+	gdb_test_no_output "macro undef USER_MACRO_C"
+    }
+}
